cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PersianEval: An Open-Source Benchmark for Evaluating LLMs on Persian"
message: >-
  If you use PersianEval in your research, please cite it using this metadata.
type: software
authors:
  - alias: "PersianEval Contributors"
version: 0.2.1
date-released: "2026-11-25"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Abolfazlrwm/persianeval"
url: "https://Abolfazlrwm.github.io/persianeval/"
keywords:
  - natural language processing
  - persian
  - farsi
  - large language models
  - benchmark
  - evaluation
abstract: >-
  PersianEval is the first serious open-source benchmark for evaluating
  large language models on Persian (Farsi). It ships eight frozen,
  checksummed evaluation tasks (reasoning, reading comprehension, spelling
  and encoding, cultural knowledge, translation, RAG faithfulness, bias
  detection, and code generation with Persian comments), a reproducible
  async evaluation harness with caching and rate limiting, and a weekly
  leaderboard published via GitHub Pages.
